From 6d9c967e740fe0bbbef37a530c9bf1c482ea79e3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xavier Damman <xdamman@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:35:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(belfry): one client key, one identity, on every path

Patch 0022 refused a client key linked to another user when a bunker
connection is created for it. The same rule now holds wherever a client
key gets linked to an authorization:

- the signer's first connect with a secret: a key declared for or bound
  to an authorization of another user in the tenant is refused with
  "Client key is linked to another account", even with the right
  secret. The check and the binding run in one transaction under the
  advisory lock on the client key;
- the nostr-login approval, which now creates its authorization with
  create_bound_to_client and answers invalid_request for such a key.

A first connect also records the key as the authorization's
client_pubkey, so disconnecting the client does not free the key for
another account (only that client can connect to it again). Revoked
and expired authorizations keep counting. Team authorizations are not
covered. No schema change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VBwxbHakpn87bGAgr3M5Ak
